#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:2
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:103
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/unit-questions-and-answers.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "Movement"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Units move when given an xref:command.adoc#orders[order] or by using "
"xref:command.adoc#initative-movement[initiative] in the Command [.edit]#& "
"Initative# phase as explained in the xref:command.adoc[Command [.edit]#& "
"Initiative# section].  Units can also move in the "
"xref:shooting.adoc[Shooting] or xref:combat.adoc[Combat] phases as explained "
"in the corresponding rules sections. This section covers all the general "
"movement rules for units including rules for various types of terrain. Rules "
"for moving characters can be found under the xref:characters.adoc#character-"
"movement[Generals, Heroes and Wizards] section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Movement distances"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:35
msgid ""
"[.bo5a]#The maximum distance a unit can move depends upon its troop type and "
"formation. Some troops are naturally faster than others – cavalry are faster "
"than infantry, for example.# Troops arranged in a regular <<formation>> are "
"able to move more quickly than units in an irregular formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Broadly speaking, infantry units and monsters move up to 20cm at a time, "
"cavalry and chariots move 30cm and artillery, such as stone throwers and "
"cannons, move 10cm. Flying troops can move up to 100cm but their movement is "
"governed by special rules, as xref:flying-units.adoc[described later].  The "
"chart below gives the full pace move distances for each troop type plus the "
"half pace movement. In each case, distances are maximums and the player can "
"move the unit a shorter distance if he wishes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Movement Chart"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|Types |Full Pace |Half Pace\n"
"\n"
"|Infantry     |20cm  |10cm\n"
"|Cavalry      |30cm  |15cm\n"
"|Chariots     |30cm  |15cm\n"
"|Artillery    |10cm  |5cm\n"
"|Monsters     |20cm  |10cm\n"
"|Machines   2+|Varies – See the [.edit]#xref:revolution:armies:index.adoc[Army Lists]#\n"
"|Flying Units |100cm |10cm\n"
"|Characters   |60cm  |60cm\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:64
msgid ""
"You’ll find a few exceptions to these moves in the army lists later in the "
"book but for now we don’t need to worry about these oddities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:86
msgid ""
"Each unit must be arranged in formation. By this we mean that all the stands "
"in the unit are placed in touch so they form a *line*, *column* or "
"*irregular* formation, as described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:99
msgid ""
"Units *charging* or *evading* can move up to full pace regardless of their "
"formation. <<the-charge,Charge>> and <<the-evade,evade>> moves are described "
"later in this section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:106
msgid ""
"All units wholly or partially in a fortified position at the start of their "
"movement can only move at half pace regardless of their formation unless "
"they are charging or evading, in which case they move at full pace as noted "
"above. [.bo5a]#See xref:shooting.adoc#defended-fortified-targets[Shooting] "
"and xref:combat.adoc#defended-fortified-troops[Combat] for more about "
"defended and fortified units.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:112
msgid ""
"Units arranged in a *column* with stands placed one behind the other (as "
"shown in picture below), either edge-to-edge or corner-to-corner, can move "
"at full pace unless in a fortified position as noted above.  Units in a "
"column are said to be in a *regular* formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a column stands are placed behind each other either edge to edge (as on the left) or so that they touch at a point forming a curved column (as on the unit following the road). This formation is primarily suited to movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:120
msgid ""
"Units arranged in a straight *line* with all their stands facing in the same "
"direction and butted edge-to-edge move at full pace unless in a fortified "
"position, as noted earlier.  Units in a line are said to be in a *regular* "
"formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "Infantry and cavalry arranged into a straight line. This is the most effective fighting formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:134
msgid ""
"All units in other formations or circumstances move at half pace. For "
"example, infantry are able to move up to 10cm, cavalry up to 15cm and so on. "
"This represents the fact that the unit is out of regular formation and that "
"it is necessary to regroup in order to move. For convenience, we refer to "
"all these formations as *irregular*. Note that the only situation where an "
"irregular formation moves at full pace is when it charges or evades."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units in irregular formations move at half pace to represent the fact that their ranks are disrupted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:144
msgid ""
"In some circumstances, units move a distance determined by rolling dice or "
"by the results of combat (such as xref:shooting.adoc#driving-back-"
"enemies[drive backs], xref:combat.adoc#retreats[retreat moves] and "
"xref:combat.adoc#advance[advances]). These distances are not affected by the "
"unit’s formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "The move"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:157
msgid ""
"When moving a unit, move each stand one at a time.  Experienced players "
"usually find it convenient and quicker to move whole units at once but in "
"principle, stands always move one at a time to ensure a path can be traced."
msgstr ""

#.  Ancients/Bo5a: Paragraph break added
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:166
msgid ""
"Select one stand from the unit and move it. Then move the second stand into "
"formation with it. Then move the third to complete the formation (assuming a "
"unit of three stands). Note there is no need for the unit to retain its "
"original formation – the stands are simply re-arranged as needed when the "
"unit moves."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: add diagram (Ancients) and "See".
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:173
msgid ""
"All stands must be able to trace a clear path to their position in the "
"unit’s final formation. Stands do not have to move to their front – they can "
"move backwards, to the side, at an angle or in any orientation or direction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stands in the same unit must touch but can be arranged into any formation you like."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:185
msgid ""
"No part of a stand can move further than its permitted maximum movement "
"distance. Always measure from the part of the stand that moves the greatest "
"distance – this will often be one of the corners."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: add diagrem (Ancients) and "See"
#.  "Even where they belong" moved after.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:200
msgid ""
"A stand cannot move through the base area of a stand from *another* unit "
"whether friend or foe either wholly or in part. A stand can move through "
"other stands of the *same* unit if they have not yet moved and are not "
"engaged in combat. This allows stands to move out of their own unit’s "
"formation without jamming each other.  A stand cannot move through other "
"stands who have already moved or are engaged in combat, even where they "
"belong to the same unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:205
msgid ""
"Stands can move through terrain appropriate to their type as noted below. "
"Stands cannot move through terrain if it is impenetrable to their type.  See "
"the section on <<terrain>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:210
msgid ""
"There is an exception to the rule that prevents stands moving through other "
"units – this happens when a unit bursts through another during an evade and "
"is <<the-path-of-evaders,described later>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:213
msgid ""
"Stands can always move through characters as described in the "
"xref:characters.adoc[Generals, Heroes and Wizards section]."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:218
msgid ""
"The Q&A has a xref:questions-and-answers.adoc#movement-questions[section on "
"Movement] with further examples, including pivoting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:225
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moving through gaps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:232
msgid ""
"When a stand moves, it can be oriented to pass through any gap so long as "
"the gap is at least as wide as the stand’s shortest edge, usually this will "
"be 20mm. For example, an infantry stand might be turned to its side to move "
"through a gap between impassable walls and a river."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:253
msgid ""
"Except as noted later, a stand cannot pass through a gap between any of the "
"following unless the gap is *wider* than the stand’s *frontage*: two enemy "
"stands, an enemy stand and a friendly stand, or an enemy stand and "
"impassable terrain. This means that the gaps must be more than 40mm for "
"infantry and more than 20mm for cavalry.  [.wmr]#See <<move-through-gap>> "
"and <<cannot-move-through-gap>>.#"
msgstr ""

#.  TODO check? Ancients has some extra here.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:262
msgid ""
"This rule prevents units moving through gaps whilst close to enemy units and "
"where there is little room for effective manoeuvring. Note that although "
"stands are not permitted to pass between enemy stands as described, this "
"does not prevent them moving between such stands to charge them, assuming "
"there is room to do so (See <<the-charge,The Charge>>)."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: Low-priority diagram text
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Infantry move through a gap – this is allowed so long as the gap is at least 20mm wide. The unit has been moved into a column – but stands could equally well be placed into a line or in irregular formation within the defile."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: Low-priority diagram text
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "This infantry unit cannot move through the gap between the two enemy units. A gap between enemy or between enemy and impassable terrain must be wider than a stand’s front for it to pass through."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:278
msgid "→ Moved to <<terrain>> at the end of this chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moving by initiative"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:286
msgid ""
"→ Moved to xref:command.adoc#initiative-movement[Command, Initiative "
"movement]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "The evade"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:305
msgid ""
"An evade is a deliberate attempt to avoid an enemy by using initiative to "
"move away. Evading units always move directly away from the closest enemy "
"they can see."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:309
msgid ""
"Evading units can move up to a full pace move regardless of their formation. "
"They can move less if they want."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:317
msgid ""
"When we say ‘directly away’ or, for that matter, ‘directly towards’, the "
"direction is established by placing a tape measure between the closest "
"points of the closest two opposing stands. Where stands are equally close, "
"the evading player may choose between them. The resulting line indicates the "
"exact direction in which the evaders move. See <<evade-direction>>."
msgstr ""

#. Move the evading unit one stand at a time. First, move
#. the evading stand that is closest to the enemy.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:332
msgid ""
"[.bo5a]#Move the evading stand that is closest to the enemy first.# This "
"stand must move in a straight line in the indicated direction directly away "
"from the evaded enemy. The stand can be oriented to face any direction "
"during its move allowing the evaders to move through gaps, turn to face "
"their enemy, or change the stand’s final facing. Move the rest of the stands "
"one stand at a time and arrange them into the unit’s new formation. Remember "
"to take into account any necessary distance required to reorient stands as "
"they move."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: Low-priority diagram text
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "The evaders move in a line established by placing a tape measure between the closest points of the closest stands – in this case A and B."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:343
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Light Cavalry:* a Cavalry unit with 6+ Armour can\n"
"evade in any direction, not just directly away from\n"
"the enemy. Note that it is still obliged to move in a\n"
"straight line when evading.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:349
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Light Infantry:* when a unit is burst through\n"
"by an infantry unit with 0 or 6+ Armour and a\n"
"ranged attack, it is only confused on the roll of 6.\n"
"However, the evading infantry unit cannot perform\n"
"a supporting charge in the same turn.\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Bo5A says 1cm, not 5.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:357
msgid ""
"Evading units cannot move through terrain they could not normally enter, nor "
"through enemy units or combat engagements. An evading unit must end its move "
"at least 5cm from any enemy unit or any unit engaged in combat.  If unable "
"to comply, units cannot evade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:368
msgid ""
"An evading unit can move through a friendly unengaged unit if the player "
"wishes assuming the evaders have sufficient move to pass completely through. "
"This is called a *burst through* and is an exception to the normal rule that "
"units can’t move through each other. The burst through represents a "
"situation where trained troops in good order manoeuvre through each other, "
"one unit opening up its ranks to allow the other to pass. See <<evade-burst-"
"through>>. This obviously takes time, so a unit which is burst through is "
"automatically *confused*! See the xref::confusion.adoc[Confusion section]."
msgstr ""

#.  New caption added, diagram text altered slightly for grammar.
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:370
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaders bursting through a friendly unit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:382
msgid ""
"→ Moved to xref:command.adoc#character-movement[Command, Character movement]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:388
#, no-wrap
msgid "The charge"
msgstr ""

#.  Moved from Combat chapter (was Moving Chargers)
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:396
msgid ""
"The rules for moving chargers may look a bit intimidating at first but do "
"not worry! Almost all moves happen in an obvious way. Many of the following "
"rules are intended to overcome any unusual circumstances you might come "
"across where care may be needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:409
msgid ""
"The term ‘charge’ describes a unit’s movement into contact with an enemy "
"unit during the Command [.edit]#& Initiative# phase whether by initiative or "
"by means of an order.  Units which move by initiative are moved before units "
"which move by orders but, apart from this, there is no obligation to move "
"charging units in any particular order.  Charges occur throughout the "
"Command [.edit]#& Initiative# phase as units move against enemy units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:416
msgid ""
"Where a charge is intended, the player must say so before any stands are "
"moved as this alerts both players to the need for care. A unit is not "
"obliged to charge just because the player has stated it – the move may prove "
"impossible or player might simply change his mind for any reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:420
msgid ""
"During a charge, each stand can move up to its full pace distance regardless "
"of the unit’s formation at the start of the move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:438
msgid ""
"At least one stand from the charging unit must be able to see the target "
"enemy unit at the start of the unit’s charge move. If none of a unit’s "
"stands can see the intended target then it cannot charge it.  [.bo5a]#See "
"the section on xref:game-values#visibility-on-the-battlefield[Visibility on "
"the battlefield]#.  Note that because units move one after the other it is "
"possible for one unit’s move to clear or block the line of sight for "
"another; it is therefore important to take care when deciding which units to "
"move and in what sequence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:442
#, no-wrap
msgid "Front, flank and rear"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:449
msgid ""
"The charging unit can potentially contact against the front, side or rear of "
"an enemy — this is an important distinction because stands suffer a penalty "
"if enemy are fighting to their side or rear as described in the "
"xref:combat.adoc#enemy-facing-own-side-or-rear[Combat] section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:457
msgid ""
"For the purpose of working out where to position units during a charge, the "
"area around each stand is divided into four zones as shown on [.edit]#<<zone-"
"infantry>> and <<zone-cavalry>>#.  The division between each zone bisects "
"the corners of the stand at the angle of 135 degrees relative to the edge.  "
"Zones are self evident in most situations and can be checked using a simple "
"guide if necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:471
msgid ""
"Once a unit’s intention to charge has been declared, begin by considering "
"the position of the entire charging unit relative to the *closest visible "
"stand* in the target unit. If the charging unit begins its move in the "
"stand’s front zone then it charges to the front, if it begins to the stand’s "
"flank it charges in the side, and if it begins to the rear it charges in the "
"rear. See <<charge-move-1>>."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling e.g.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:481
msgid ""
"If the charging unit is not entirely within a single zone then it counts as "
"being in the zone that it mostly occupies. So, if a unit is between the "
"front and flank but the greater proportion is to the front, the unit counts "
"as in the front. If a unit is positioned in such a way that it is exactly "
"divided between two zones then roll a dice to decide – e.g. 1, 2, or 3 the "
"front; 4, 5, or 6 the side. See <<charge-move-2>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:495
msgid ""
"In most situations it is a simple matter to position the charging unit "
"against the indicated front, side, or rear edge of the enemy unit. In some "
"cases extra care is called for. Players who are unfamiliar with the game "
"should make a point of moving the stands one at a time, as described below, "
"until they are used to the placement rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:500
msgid ""
"To begin, the charging player selects one stand from the charging unit. Any "
"stand may be chosen – it does not have to be the closest. This stand must be "
"able to see the enemy and must have a clear path to the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:504
msgid ""
"The selected charging stand is moved into place against the enemy stand that "
"has already been identified as the closest visible stand to the charging "
"unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:511
msgid ""
"Move the charging stand so that its front edge contacts the appropriate edge "
"of the enemy stand. If the unit is charging from the front zone, place the "
"charger against the enemy stand’s front edge.  [.bo5a]#If it is charging "
"from the flank, place the charger against the side. If from the rear, place "
"the charger against the rear edge.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:534
msgid ""
"If possible, place the charging stand exactly centre-to-centre against the "
"edge of the target stand – see <<maximise-frontage-1>>. If this is "
"impossible, for whatever reason, see <<unable-to-contact-centre-to-centre>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:555
msgid ""
"Once the first charging stand has been positioned, the remaining stands are "
"placed one at a time to make a line formation or ‘battle line’. Each stand "
"must be able to trace a line to its new position as it moves. Note that it "
"doesn’t matter what formation the unit is in when it begins its charge, "
"charging units always form a battle line if they can do so [.bo5a]#– if they "
"are unable to do so then see <<unable-to-form-a-battle-line>> below.#"
msgstr ""

#. Stands are placed into a coherent formation as they move.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:564
msgid ""
"[.bo5a]#To form the battle line,# place the second stand beside the first, "
"and place the third stand beside either the first or second. You cannot "
"leave a gap in the battle line and then fill it later. The reason for "
"breaking down movement by individual stands is to make sure each stand has "
"an accessible route to its final place in the battle line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:576
msgid ""
"Each stand must be placed in the battle line in such a way that as much of "
"its front edge as possible makes contact with the enemy. This is called "
"‘*maximising frontage*’. If it is impossible to place a stand into the "
"battle line so that its front edge makes contact with an enemy, then it must "
"be placed so that its front corner touches an enemy if it can. This means "
"that the maximum number of charging stands will be drawn into the combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:591
msgid ""
"If there are other enemy units adjacent to the target unit then the "
"obligation to ‘maximise frontage’ extends to these other units too. So, "
"where there is another enemy stand aligned to the target unit, a charging "
"stand must be placed against this second enemy if this is its only way to "
"*maximise frontage*. However, chargers will always maximise frontage against "
"the unit they *originally* charged where they can do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:597
msgid ""
"Any additional units contacted by charging stands count as being charged and "
"are drawn into the combat engagement – even if they are only touching corner-"
"to-corner.  If armed with appropriate weapons they can shoot at the chargers "
"as described in the xref:shooting.adoc#shooting-at-charging-enemy[Shooting "
"section]."
msgstr ""

#.  Moved from Combat section.  It's maybe not ideal to have
#.  support mentioned here, but it's already in this general
#.  section under Enveloping Charge.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:614
msgid ""
"During the Command phase, an [.edit]#infantry# unit is allowed to make a "
"supporting charge if it is positioned behind another [.edit]#infantry unit# "
"so that at least one stand could theoretically support in combat from the "
"rear.  [.edit]#(See xref:combat.adoc#supporting-troops[Supporting troops] in "
"the Combat section.)#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:620
msgid ""
"If the front unit charges, whether on initiative or by means of an order, "
"then the second unit can automatically make a supporting charge. It can do "
"so whether the first unit charges on initiative or with an order, even where "
"the second unit was not included in a brigade order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:629
msgid ""
"Note that the second unit might have more or fewer stands than the charging "
"unit, or it could have some stands positioned to give rear support and some "
"not.  Regardless of how stands are positioned, only one unit can make a "
"supporting charge on behalf of another. It is not possible to place two "
"units so that they can both make supporting charges – in such a situation, "
"the player must choose which unit will make the supporting charge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:636
msgid ""
"The supporting charge is a normal move, except the unit making the "
"supporting charge must be placed so that it touches the first unit and at "
"least one stand supports it either from the rear or side. No stands can be "
"placed into [.edit]#contact# with enemies – neither into edge contact nor "
"corner-to-corner contact."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:648
msgid ""
"The supporting charge is a special kind of combined move – the supporting "
"unit’s move is rolled into that of the charging unit and is considered part "
"of it. The charger can be thought of as carrying the supporting charger with "
"the same order. If a unit is unable to move for whatever reason (if it is "
"confused for example), or if it does not have sufficient move distance to "
"move (if it is in irregular formation for example) then it cannot make a "
"supporting charge. Also note, that after *failing* to receive its *first "
"order* a unit cannot use its half pace move to join combat by moving into "
"the *supporting position*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:661
msgid ""
"In some situations the proximity of scenery or other stands makes it "
"impossible to position all the chargers exactly as described. In some cases "
"this may mean the charge is not permitted, in others that chargers can be "
"repositioned to accommodate the situation. These circumstances are covered "
"in the following rules sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:672
msgid ""
"The first charging stand is always positioned centre-to-centre with the "
"closest enemy stand where possible.  If this is not possible then the first "
"charging stand is positioned as closely to centre-to-centre as it can go, "
"but there must be at least 1 full centimetre of exposed stand edge to "
"contact against."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:676
msgid ""
"If there is less than 1 cm of exposed edge then the stand is not an eligible "
"target because it is ‘blocked’. <<blocked-edges,See below>> for how to deal "
"with blocked stands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:697
msgid ""
"If a stand has insufficient room or insufficient move distance to form a "
"straight battle line, it must be placed either directly behind, or beside "
"and staggered back from a stand that has already moved. Stands placed behind "
"must be positioned facing the same direction as the stand in front of them. "
"Stands that are staggered back can be placed with as much or as little of "
"their stands touching as the player wishes, but must contact with a fellow "
"stand at least corner to corner. Either way the unit must retain a coherent "
"formation with all stands touching. If a unit is unable to both charge *and* "
"retain a coherent formation then the move is not allowed. See <<f-unable-to-"
"form-a-battle-line>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:705
msgid ""
"Any additional enemy units contacted as a result of the placement of these "
"stands also count as being charged and are drawn into the combat engagement "
"– even if chargers are only touching at their side or rear edge.  If armed "
"with appropriate shooting weapons they are entitled to shoot at the charging "
"unit as described in the xref:shooting.adoc#shooting-at-charging-"
"enemy[Shooting section]."
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling available
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:723
msgid ""
"In some situations a charging unit will be unable to charge because, "
"although it can see the enemy unit, the indicated edge of the closest stand "
"is blocked.  The indicated edge could conceivably be blocked by impassable "
"terrain, by other enemy stands, or by stands from other friendly units that "
"have already engaged the enemy unit in combat. Remember, an edge is blocked "
"not only if it is completely covered, but also if there is less than 1cm of "
"exposed edge available to contact."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:729
msgid ""
"In all these situations the charger moves the charging stand against the "
"next closest stand in the target unit, assuming this stand is an accessible "
"visible stand within the same zone. If this stand edge is also blocked then "
"the charger can move to the third closest stand, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:738
msgid ""
"If no accessible edge is presented by any stand in the target unit then the "
"charge is not normally allowed – for example, if there is impassable terrain "
"covering the unit’s front edge and the charger is positioned in the target’s "
"front zone. The exception to this is a ‘pinned’ enemy unit as described "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:746
msgid ""
"If the indicated edge of the entire enemy target unit has already been "
"covered by stands from other friendly units then the unit is described as "
"*pinned*."
msgstr ""

#. // Difference with Bo5A/Ancients
#. [.bo5a]#Note that *all* appropriate
#. edges have to be covered by opposing stands – not by a mix of
#. opposing stands and terrain for example.#
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:760
msgid ""
"In the case of a pinned target, the first charging unit can move into corner-"
"to-corner contact with the closest enemy stand assuming the charger can see "
"it and has a clear path.  This is an exception to the normal rule that "
"stands must charge edge-to-edge. See <<f-pinned-target>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:780
msgid ""
"If the target unit is in irregular formation then it might not be possible "
"for all the charging stands to engage by forming a conventional battle line. "
"In this case the first charging stand is placed in the standard way as "
"already described. It is only the remaining chargers that are placed "
"differently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:784
msgid ""
"Remaining charging stands are placed in a line but staggered to the front or "
"rear so that they follow the shape of the stands presented by the enemy unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:790
msgid ""
"Although these charging stands might touch the enemy only at a corner or "
"along part of their front edge, they are considered to be maximising "
"frontage so long as they have the maximum portion of enemy stand directly to "
"their front."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:804
msgid ""
"The ‘envelop’ rule applies when a unit is charged in the side or rear – it "
"represents a unit’s inability to turn enough troops quickly enough to avoid "
"being enveloped by an enemy charge. The reason for this rule is to avoid "
"situations where it is otherwise disadvantageous to charge a unit in the "
"side because only a single stand can touch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:815
msgid ""
"When a unit charges an enemy unit from the flank or rear and contacts only "
"against the side or rear of an enemy stand or stands, then any charging "
"stands that would not otherwise touch the enemy when forming a battle line "
"are allowed to make a further move into contact with the charged enemy unit "
"xref:combat.adoc#basic-pursuit[as described for a pursuit]. Stands must have "
"sufficient move distance remaining from their charge move to make the "
"envelopment move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:829
msgid ""
"This is called an ‘enveloping charge’ and it is entirely up to the charger "
"whether to envelop or form a conventional battle line. Each stand enveloping "
"in this way must move so that its front edge contacts the charged enemy "
"unit, otherwise these stands can be positioned as the player wishes so long "
"as they remain in formation. Enveloping stands can contact other enemy units "
"and therefore bring them into the combat, but they must also contact the "
"charged unit either to their front edge or front corner as described. Note "
"that this is comparable to a normal xref:combat.adoc#basic-pursuit[pursuit "
"move] in most respects – the enveloping charge effectively combines a charge "
"and pursuit into a single move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:834
msgid ""
"If chargers are infantry with supporting chargers then move both the "
"charging and supporting units and work out any shooting first. Supporting "
"units remain in their battle line and do not envelope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:847
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units which move off the table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:854
msgid ""
"Sometimes units or characters are obliged to move off the table. This can "
"happen when a unit receives a ‘xref:characters.adoc#blunders[blundered]’ "
"order but can also happen to units that are "
"xref:combat.adoc#retreat[defeated in combat] or troops "
"xref:shooting.adoc#driving-back-enemies[driven back] by missile fire or "
"magic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:863
msgid ""
"If one or more stands in a unit leaves the table edge, whether wholly or "
"partially the whole unit leaves the table. Units that leave the table as a "
"result of retreating from combat are deemed destroyed. In any other "
"situation roll a D6 and then consult the table below to see what happens. "
"Deduct −1 from the roll for each of the unit’s stands that has already been "
"removed as a casualty and apply the result immediately."
msgstr ""

#.  Difference: Ancients says no initiative moves for 5-6, orders only.
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:889
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|D6 |Result\n"
"\n"
"|0 or less\n"
"|The unit/character leaves the battlefield and\n"
"does not return. The unit/character is\n"
"considered to have been destroyed.\n"
"\n"
"|1–2\n"
"|The unit/character leaves the battlefield and\n"
"may or may not reappear. At the start of its\n"
"side’s next turn, before initiative moves are\n"
"made, roll again on this chart.\n"
"\n"
"|3–4\n"
"|The unit/character reappears at the table edge\n"
"at the same point it left. The unit/character\n"
"cannot move further that turn.\n"
"\n"
"|5–6\n"
"|The unit/character reappears at the same\n"
"point on the table edge it left from. If it is\n"
"reappearing at the beginning of a turn, it may\n"
"move as normal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. //
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:896
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When a unit reappears on the table it must retain the\n"
"same formation and face the same direction as when it\n"
"left the table.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Difference: Ancients says rear edge against the table edge, facing forward.
#. //
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:899
msgid "Infantry in line or column, cavalry in a line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:912
msgid ""
"Characters who move off the table with units they have joined suffer the "
"same fate as the unit. Characters who are on their own must roll in the "
"unlikely event that they leave the table.  If a General leaves the table "
"(for whatever reason) and does not return immediately then the battle is "
"over and his army withdraws. He abandons his army and heads for the hills "
"and is considered to be a casualty. See the xref:end-of-the-battle.adoc[End "
"of the Battle] section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:920
#, no-wrap
msgid "====\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:926
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The _Advanced Terrain_ rules in the rulebook extend the basic _Terrain_\n"
"rules, they do not replace them. The two sections have been combined\n"
"here.\n"
"\n"
"See the 2025 xref:questions-and-answers.adoc[].\n"
"====\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Removed "In the Advanced Terrain Rules the"
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:938
msgid ""
"By terrain we mean woods, hills, rivers and other features that might "
"conceivably be found on the battlefields.  Many of these features hinder "
"troops because they impose a Command penalty. In some cases, features can be "
"impenetrable to one or more troop types.  [.edit]#This can# radically affect "
"strategy, providing strong points to defend as well as obstructions to "
"movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:944
msgid ""
"Terrain features are classified by characteristics such as accessibility and "
"other effects they provide for the troops. The characteristics are described "
"as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:945
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passable terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:947
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Standard terrain that does not impede\n"
"movement or provide any advantage to units crossing it.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:950
msgid "Accessible to all troop types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:951
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rough terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:955
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Challenging terrain that complicates\n"
"movement and prevents the use of charge bonuses.\n"
"While it hinders attackers, it does not provide a defensive\n"
"advantage.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:961
msgid ""
"Accessible to Infantry, Monsters, and Cavalry. Charging units do not receive "
"charge bonuses against enemy stands at least partially in Rough Terrain. "
"Defenders are not considered defended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:962
#, no-wrap
msgid "Difficult terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:965
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Treacherous terrain that is unsafe for\n"
"large creatures or mounted units but provides infantry\n"
"with defensive benefits.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:969
msgid ""
"Accessible only to Infantry. Infantry stands at least partially within "
"Difficult terrain are considered defended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:970
#, no-wrap
msgid "Broken terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:972
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Highly obstructed terrain that prevents\n"
"units from forming proper ranks or moving at speed.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:976
msgid ""
"All units at least partially within Broken terrain are in Irregular "
"Formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:979
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*non-open terrain hindering orientation\n"
"and complicating commanding.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:983
msgid ""
"Units at least partially in the Dense Terrain subtract −1 to the Command "
"value when being ordered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:987
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*While individuals may traverse\n"
"this terrain, it is impossible for organised units to move\n"
"through.*\n"
msgstr ""

#.  (Breaking description list)
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:992
msgid ""
"No units may enter Impassable terrain. Mountless or flying characters and "
"flying units may pass through (or over) as long as they do not end their "
"movement inside it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:996
#, no-wrap
msgid "2cm visibility terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1000
msgid ""
"When within woods, forest or villages, troops cannot draw a line of sight "
"except that stands placed within 2cm of the edge can see out, and can be "
"seen by troops outside."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1004
msgid ""
"By the same token, troops further inside the woods, forest or village can "
"see and be seen by other troops up to 2cm away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1007
#, no-wrap
msgid "Types of terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1010
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hills and slopes"
msgstr ""

#.  Comment/question/TODO: Is this undefended from shooting?
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1017
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Passable* terrain. Blocks line of sight.\n"
"Infantry and artillery stands positioned on a hill are\n"
"xref:combat.adoc#defended[defended] against any units charging or shooting from\n"
"lower positions. Artillery units on hills can shoot over\n"
"friendly units at lower elevation.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1019
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shallow rivers or streams"
msgstr ""

#.  Comment: Sand dunes are *very* difficult to climb or cross,
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1025
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Rough*, *Dense* and *Broken*\n"
"terrain. Units charging from within or across a stream\n"
"do not receive a charge bonus. Units that have crossed\n"
"a stream suffer a −1 penalty to subsequent orders in the\n"
"same Command phase.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1028
#, no-wrap
msgid "Loose terrain, soft sand and fields"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1030
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Rough* terrain.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1031
#, no-wrap
msgid "Marsh or dunes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1033
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Rough* and *Dense* terrain.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1034
#, no-wrap
msgid "Woods and tall scrub"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1037
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Difficult* and *Dense* terrain. There is\n"
"only 2cm visibility in this type of terrain.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1038
#, no-wrap
msgid "Villages, towns, and other built-up areas"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1043
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Passable*,\n"
"*Dense* and *Broken* terrain. Infantry and artillery units\n"
"count as xref:combat.adoc#defended[*defended*] when within. All unit types\n"
"can be pursued when starting their retreat in this terrain\n"
"type. Villages and towns have visibility of 2cm.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1049
msgid ""
"Model-wise they are a bordered area consisting of a number of buildings. The "
"entire built-up area is considered to be a broad terrain type: no account is "
"taken of individual buildings, gardens, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1050
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual buildings, terrain features, sheer cliffs or mountains"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1053
msgid "These are *Impassable* terrain that blocks line of sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1054
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rivers, lakes, lava, ravines, deep water or deep pits"
msgstr ""

#.  Bo5A difference: dense terrain penalty still applies
#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1057
msgid "These are *Impassable* terrain that does not block line of sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1059
#, no-wrap
msgid "Roads and tracks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1065
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Passable* terrain. A non-flying unit\n"
"that moves its maximum movement distance in a column\n"
"formation along the road can make an extra half-pace\n"
"move and gains a +1 Command bones for a following\n"
"order in this Command phase. However, this movement\n"
"must not result in contact with the enemy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1070
msgid ""
"For a brigade to benefit from this rule, it must be at most 4cm wide (e.g. a "
"one-stand-wide infantry column or two side-by-side cavalry columns)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1071
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bridges and fords"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1075
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Passable* terrain. Bridges and fords\n"
"don't block line of sight. Bridges and fords that connect\n"
"to a road or track are part of it and all bonuses apply.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1076
#, no-wrap
msgid "Low linear obstacles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1083
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Impassable* for Chariots,\n"
"Artillery and Machines. These are features such as ditches,\n"
"hedges, fences, and low walls. Infantry and artillery\n"
"stands placed behind a low linear obstacle count as\n"
"xref:combat.adoc#defended[*defended*]. Low linear obstacles don’t\n"
"block line of sight.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1084
#, no-wrap
msgid "High linear obstacles, fortress walls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1087
msgid ""
"These are described in detail in the chapter xref:siege-and-"
"fortresses.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

