msgid "include::partial$terrain-restrictions.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units forced into impenetrable terrain"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1107
msgid ""
"The rules occasionally oblige units to move into terrain they cannot "
"[.bo5a]#enter. Stands are not permitted to move so that their bases "
"intersect with terrain that is impassable to them – either wholly or "
"partially. Stands will automatically# halt at the edge [.bo5a]#of terrain "
"they cannot enter#."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: link, and be more definite.
#. type: delimited block * 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1116
msgid ""
"If they are *driven back* into impassable terrain as a result of shooting or "
"magic, units may become *confused* (see the xref::shooting.adoc[Shooting "
"Phase] section and the xref::confusion.adoc[Confusion section]). If a unit "
"is forced to retreat into impassable terrain during combat, then stands may "
"be destroyed as a result (see xref::combat.adoc#retreats[Combat phase – "
"Retreats])."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/movement.adoc:1121
msgid ""
"The Q&A has a xref:questions-and-answers.adoc#movement-questions[section on "
"Movement] with further examples."
msgstr ""
